{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility","id":1116656,"title":"Compatibility","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-15T19:59:22-07:00","id":1116656,"title":"Compatibility","content":"Are these systems, under Chronicle of darkness, (new world of darkness, 2nd edition being formal title i believe); all able to play and interact with each other. Could I successfully run a game with a vampire, werewolf, and changeling? With only minimal effort to make sure play power levels are all with in ball park of each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13672-thecowley","name":"thecowley","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:04:18-07:00","id":1116660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility#post1116656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these systems, under Chronicle of darkness, (new world of darkness, 2nd edition being formal title i believe); all able to play and interact with each other. Could I successfully run a game with a vampire, werewolf, and changeling? With only minimal effort to make sure play power levels are all with in ball park of each other?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, you can. <br /> <br /> The whole point of having say... humans as the default instead of a supernatural was that it essentially means rules wise, all supernaturals are humans mechanically plus whatever baggage they had as part of being a supernatural.<br /> <br /> you might need to do some slight Homebrew in that some rule or power interactions might not be intended, but it's totally doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:06:56-07:00","id":1116662,"title":"","content":"so with in reason, most systems should over lap with out much difficulty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13672-thecowley","name":"thecowley","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:26:43-07:00","id":1116674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility#post1116656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these systems, under Chronicle of darkness, (new world of darkness, 2nd edition being formal title i believe);</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the formal title <i>is</i> &quot;Chronicles of Darkness?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> all able to play and interact with each other. Could I successfully run a game with a vampire, werewolf, and changeling? </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With only minimal effort to make sure play power levels are all with in ball park of each other? </div> </div> </div>Well.... &quot;minimal&quot; is the word you want to watch out. CoD games give <i>compatible </i>systems, not <i>balanced </i>systems. Even the developers acknowledge that demons, mummies, and mages in general are going to roll over everybody else.<br /> <br /> Also something of note is the definition of &quot;power level.&quot; For example, a vampire whose character concept isn't being a combat specialist will have a tough time duking it out with a werewolf. But the forte of the Kindred in general is to <i>avoid</i> getting into physical fisticuffs in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:41:21-07:00","id":1116678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1116674#post1116674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Also something of note is the definition of &quot;power level.&quot; For example, a vampire whose character concept isn't being a combat specialist will have a tough time duking it out with a werewolf. But the forte of the Kindred in general is to <i>avoid</i> getting into physical fisticuffs in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>true enough. I'm not worried if every one can fight equally per say. but that every one can shine in unique ways that seem to be of equal footing. While I expect that werewolf character to out brawl the other two, the vampire has their deceptions, and the changeling straight up charms. just examples, ive only seen the mage system so far myself<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13672-thecowley","name":"thecowley","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T21:44:07-07:00","id":1116712,"title":"","content":".<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility#post1116656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicle of darkness, (new world of darkness, 2nd edition being formal title i believe)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clear this up...<ul><li>August 2013, <i>The God-Machine Chronicle </i>was published. It was sold as a setting (or, &quot;Chronicle&quot;) book for the game that was known at the time as <i>World of Darkness </i>(colloquially as &quot;new World of Darkness&quot;), featuring optional rules updates for the game's system, the Storytelling System.</li> <li>December 2013, <i>Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle</i> was published. Like <i>The God Machine Chronicle</i>, it was sold as a setting book featuring optional rules updates to <i>Vampire: the Requiem, </i>to bring it up to date with the revisions to the core Storytelling System.</li> <li>August 2014, the updated Storytelling System were officially announced as the second edition of the Storytelling System, and became re-branded as the Revised Storytelling System. A new book, <i>World of Darkness, 2nd Edition</i> was announced, which would be a full core rulebook for the Revised Storytelling System, featuring the rules that had been presented as optional in <i>The God-Machine Chronicle</i> written in as the default rules. The Revised Storytelling System books that were under development at the time, <i>Tooth and Claw: The Idigam Chronicle</i> and <i>Mystery Play: the Fallen World Chronicle</i>, as well as the recently-announced <i>Too Solid Flesh: the Huntsman Chronicle</i>, were consequently renamed <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken, 2nd Edition,</i> <i>Mage: the Awakening, 2nd Edition</i>, and <i>Changeling: the Lost</i>,<i> 2nd Edition</i> respectively.</li> <li>December 2014, <i>Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle</i> was re-released with a new cover and new title, now being called <i>Vampire: the Requiem, 2nd Edition</i>.</li> <li>March 2015, <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken, 2nd Edition</i> was published.</li> <li>October 2015, publishing rights for<i>Classic World of Darkness</i> (known colloquially as &quot;old world of darkness&quot;), <i>World of Darkness,</i> and the other White Wolf Publishing Intellectual Properties, as well as the name &quot;White Wolf Publishing&quot; were bought from Crowd Control Productions by Paradox Interactive. They created a new subsidiary under the name White Wolf Publishing.</li> <li>December 2015, the new White Wolf Publishing changed the name of the intellectual property previously known as <i>Classic World of Darkness</i> to <i>World of Darkness</i>, and the name of the intellectual property previously known as <i>World of Darkness </i>to <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>. The book that had previously been in development under the title <i>World of Darkness, 2nd Edition</i> was consequently renamed <i>Chronicles of Darkness,</i> and released later that same year under that title.</li> </ul>So no, <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> is not formally titled<i> New World of Darkness, 2nd Edition</i>. The fist edition of <i>Chronicles of Dakness</i> is just colloquially referred to as <i>New World of Darkness</i>.I don't blame you for being confused. I would be utterly baffled myself if I hadn't been spending half my life on these forums for the past five years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-16-2017, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T21:52:41-07:00","id":1116717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1116712#post1116712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Just to clear this up...<ul><li>August 2013, <i>The God-Machine Chronicle </i>was published. It was sold as a setting (or, &quot;Chronicle&quot;) book for the game that was known at the time as <i>World of Darkness </i>(colloquially as &quot;new World of Darkness&quot;), featuring optional rules updates for the game's system, the Storytelling System.</li> <li>December 2013, <i>Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle</i> was published. Like <i>The God Machine Chronicle</i>, it was sold as a setting book featuring optional rules updates to <i>Vampire: the Requiem, </i>to bring it up to date with the revisions to the core Storytelling System.</li> <li>August 2014, the updated Storytelling System were officially announced as the second edition of the Storytelling System, and became re-branded as the Revised Storytelling System. A new book, <i>World of Darkness, 2nd Edition</i> was announced, which would be a full core rulebook for the Revised Storytelling System, featuring the rules that had been presented as optional in <i>The God-Machine Chronicle</i> written in as the default rules. The Revised Storytelling System books that were under development at the time, <i>Tooth and Claw: The Idigam Chronicle</i> and <i>Mystery Play: the Fallen World Chronicle</i>, as well as the recently-announced <i>Too Solid Flesh: the Huntsman Chronicle</i>, were consequently renamed <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken, 2nd Edition,</i> <i>Mage: the Awakening, 2nd Edition</i>, and <i>Changeling: the Lost</i>,<i> 2nd Edition</i> respectively.</li> <li>December 2014, <i>Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle</i> was re-released with a new cover and new title, now being called <i>Vampire: the Requiem, 2nd Edition</i>.</li> <li>March 2015, <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken, 2nd Edition</i> was published.</li> <li>October 2015, publishing rights for<i>Classic World of Darkness</i> (known colloquially as &quot;old world of darkness&quot;), <i>World of Darkness,</i> and the other White Wolf Publishing Intellectual Properties, as well as the name &quot;White Wolf Publishing&quot; were bought from Crowd Control Productions by Paradox Interactive. They created a new subsidiary under the name White Wolf Publishing.</li> <li>December 2015, the new White Wolf Publishing changed the name of the intellectual property previously known as <i>Classic World of Darkness</i> to <i>World of Darkness</i>, and the name of the intellectual property previously known as <i>World of Darkness </i>to <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>. The book that had previously been in development under the title <i>World of Darkness, 2nd Edition</i> was consequently renamed <i>Chronicles of Darkness,</i> and released later that same year under that title.</li> </ul>So no, <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> is not formally titled<i> New World of Darkness, 2nd Edition</i>. The fist edition of <i>Chronicles of Dakness</i> is just colloquially referred to as <i>New World of Darkness</i>.I don't blame you for being confused. I would be utterly baffled myself if I hadn't been spending half my life on these forums for the past five years.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks for the explanation, will help me in describing it to my other newcomers to the system as well<br /> <br /> may I also venture a guess that any of the line published after 2014 are the ones meant to be interchangeable with each other<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13672-thecowley","user":"thecowley","date":". 07-16-2017, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13672-thecowley","name":"thecowley","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T23:09:10-07:00","id":1116740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1116712#post1116712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.Just to clear this up...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> , I <i>really</i> think this post should be made like sticky to main boards and just be quoted for everyone asking this kind question. You really nailed it here - just do not let to make it go away with topics flood in coming weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T23:54:03-07:00","id":1116748,"title":"","content":"So, I've actually played in a crossover game, so let me offer my advice.<br /> <br /> The games systems are not balanced, but that doesn't mean they aren't fair. Let me explain.<br /> <br /> I played the sole vampire in a game with two werewolves, a beast, and a mage. I was also the character with the lowest supernatural tolerance.<br /> <br /> While the other characters were more powerful, I had more merits, and thus more connections to get us out of trouble (vampires in general have some really awesome merits that are focused on mortal society).<br /> <br /> Let me point out my proudest moment in the game. Our mage was trapped in a time loop of shifting sands by a master of time. He was unable to escape, but then I walked onto the scene. My BP 1 vampire used dominate 1 to defeat this master of time; &quot;Don't Cast Magic&quot; is a three sentence phrase. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So as I said, the systems may not be balanced, but that doesn't mean they aren't fair.<br /> <br /> (We ruled using mana to clear mental conditions as casting magic, for those who might not understand why the mage didn't just clear mesmerize. We also ruled that they had to actually know about the possibility of a condition, and dominate is very subtle.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:41:51-07:00","id":1117110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1116748#post1116748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've actually played in a crossover game, so let me offer my advice.<br /> <br /> The games systems are not balanced, but that doesn't mean they aren't fair. Let me explain.<br /> <br /> I played the sole vampire in a game with two werewolves, a beast, and a mage. I was also the character with the lowest supernatural tolerance.<br /> <br /> While the other characters were more powerful, I had more merits, and thus more connections to get us out of trouble (vampires in general have some really awesome merits that are focused on mortal society).<br /> <br /> Let me point out my proudest moment in the game. Our mage was trapped in a time loop of shifting sands by a master of time. He was unable to escape, but then I walked onto the scene. My BP 1 vampire used dominate 1 to defeat this master of time; &quot;Don't Cast Magic&quot; is a three sentence phrase. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So as I said, the systems may not be balanced, but that doesn't mean they aren't fair.<br /> <br /> (We ruled using mana to clear mental conditions as casting magic, for those who might not understand why the mage didn't just clear mesmerize. We also ruled that they had to actually know about the possibility of a condition, and dominate is very subtle.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much what i meant. I figured each creature/pc type/race would have its one advantages, but so long as they mesh well enough, I can make it work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13672-thecowley","name":"thecowley","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T01:35:13-07:00","id":1117127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1117110#post1117110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pretty much what i meant. I figured each creature/pc type/race would have its one advantages, but so long as they mesh well enough, I can make it work</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you know what you're doing then you can make it work. However, if you're gonna run a crossover game then I'd suggest having everyone make characters together so that there isn't a lot of overlap.<br /> <br /> Like vampires in general have some of the best merits socially, but mages with certain arcana can just cast a spell (admittedly at the highest levels) to have social mertis without spending xp on them. I believe werewolves also have some gifts and rites that affect organizations, while in general vampires have to rely on the merits.<br /> <br /> So the real challenge to a crossover game isn't balancing the systems (don't try it, just trust me on this one), it's keeping every player relevant and giving each one a time to shine.<br /> <br /> Though I think there is supposed to be a crossover chronicle coming out at some point (admittedly, I know next to nothing about it). So, when that comes out that should provide some helpful tips, and probably some good stories as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T02:53:33-07:00","id":1117131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1117110#post1117110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what i meant. I figured each creature/pc type/race would have its one advantages, but so long as they mesh well enough, I can make it work</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend having all the players play the same splat. The different splats are designed for certain types of games with different themes, and most splats have their unique social conditions and goals that won't mesh well.<br /> Vampires will have a hard time doing anything during the day. Werewolves need to have contact with Spirits or they won't be able to buy Renown and unlock new Gifts. Mages will outshine all other splats (except Mummy and Demon) in the areas they're good at. Changelings are hunted by their Keeper and by Huntsmen. Demons are hiding en masse from the God-Machine and spend most of their time trying to mess around with it in various ways.<br /> The different gamelines are compatible ruleswise as in a cabal of mages can run into a throng of prometheans and start obsessing over this new mystery or a vampire NPC has joined the PCs' pack of werewolves for whatever reason, but the themes and challenges in one gameline are specifically designed for that particular splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T04:32:05-07:00","id":1117142,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness splats are a bit like Bionicle sets. If you want to connect them together all the components will fit, but the end result might not be pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:19:32-07:00","id":1117203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1117142#post1117142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness splats are a bit like Bionicle sets. If you want to connect them together all the components will fit, but the end result might not be pretty.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when you <i>do</i> manage to make it work, it looks fuckin' <i>awesome</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:32:20-07:00","id":1117208,"title":"","content":"I <i>do </i>recommend crossovers, though, once you're familiar with the gamelines.<br /> (If you're not familiar with them you risk getting overwhelmed by all the splat specific rules.)<br /> We've had great fun doing ventures into the Shadow and mucking about with werewolves in our Vampire campaign (as well as broking shady deals with the Seers, exploring different branches of TFV, going on expeditions in the Underworld, etc). Mage is literally built for exploring mysteries and the other gamelines are ripe with them. The Pack (a Werewolf sourcebok) is a great source for how other splats might join and take part of a pack. I remember seeing that a demon can take another supernatural creature as a Cover.<br /> <br /> Edit: What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-17-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:22:07-07:00","id":1117242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1116717#post1116717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks for the explanation, will help me in describing it to my other newcomers to the system as well<br /> <br /> may I also venture a guess that any of the line published after 2014 are the ones meant to be interchangeable with each other</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they were meant to be interoperable from the original publication starting in 2004 (the first edition of Chronicles of Darkness, at the time branded World of Darkness). The 2nd edition material will work with each other as well. <br /> <br /> It is also possible to mix 1st and 2nd edition material with some work on your end as well. The edition changes are not so drastic as to make it impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:12:19-07:00","id":1117294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1117242#post1117242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, they were meant to be interoperable from the original publication starting in 2004 (the first edition of Chronicles of Darkness, at the time branded World of Darkness). The 2nd edition material will work with each other as well.<br /> <br /> It is also possible to mix 1st and 2nd edition material with some work on your end as well. The edition changes are not so drastic as to make it impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. the core rules are close to the same, close enough that you can use a lot of things mostly unchanged, at least for mortals, save for some new optional systems like Social Maneuvering or Investigation. A few things to note per gameline:<ul><li>Vampire rules remain close to the same, but the disciplines have been noticeably boosted, and it seems Bloodlines are moving away from unique disciplines in favor of Bloodline-specific devotions, although we haven't seen many Bloodlines in 2E material as of yet. Honestly, I feel like the Bloodline Disciplines vs. Devotions would come down to the Bloodline. If you've got a really esoteric Bloodline with really unique powers, a Discipline might be in order. If you have a Bloodline that expands upon or twists the abilities of a Clan, I'd say go with Devotions.</li> <li>Werewolf has some of the more radical changes, with Harmony being a two-ended scale now, where the middle is generally more desirable, rather than being just a Karma meter. Additionally, Gifts have been pretty significantly re-jiggered, so now it's a Gift with five Facets, each keyed to a Renown. When you get a new Gift, you get a free Facet, when you increase your Renown, you get a new Facet from one of your Gifts, keyed to the Renown you've raised, and taking a Facet requires you have access to that Gift, and at least 1 dot in the right Renown. They also removed Unihar due to the numerous unfortunate implications, and now the term &quot;Ghost Wolf&quot; refers to Tribeless Werewolves. I also like 2E Wolf-blooded, especially since you can become one spontaneously from Lunacy, and there are Tells to make you a more classic Werwolf. And theoretically, you can become a major splat with both its own Supernatural Tolerance, <i>and</i> a dot of Primal Urge. Which I'm sure can lead to some fun shenanigans, and could make for a good Mystery for Mages.</li> <li>Mage has significantly eased the process of Creative thaumaturgy, simplified spell rolls, and is just generally easier to play. Moreover, they've expanded Attainments so the spells that <i>everyone</i> wants (e.g. the various Mage Armor) are now Attainments that can be bought with Experiences, are usable at any time without risking Paradox, and don't eat up your spell capacity.</li> <li>Promethean has another set of big changes. Humanity has been replaced with Pilgrimage, which rises as you progress toward humanity; Refinements are broken up into roles, and you need to fulfill at least 8 roles, up to 10, from a mix of various Refinements, to complete your Pilgrimage (completing the full 10 improves your chances). Transmutations have been totally reworked. Centimanus Transmutations are totally gone, and Centimani pick up Dread Powers instead. All the other Transmutations have been changed from an \u00e0 la carte menus of powers to a single set of four powers, called Alembics, in a series. You can Charge them by spending 1 to 4 Pyros to charge them for the scene (charging an Alembic also charges all those before it), and your access to a Transmutation is contingent on your current Refinement, though you can spend Vitriol to calcify a Transmutation so you can keep it after changing Refinement.</li> <li>Changeling 2E isn't out yet, but what we've seen sa far has shown that Clarity is a lot more likely to rise or drop in a game, with specific triggers based on your Seeming. Kiths are also less coupled to Seeming, with Kiths being what you were used for by your Fairie masters and Seemings being linked to how you escaped. Contracts have also been restructured, but I can't recall exactly how, and I my laptop is being really bitchy with Google Drive so I can't get to the compiled previews. They've also introduced a new antagonist called the Huntsmen, which are basically Mr. Meeseeks plus Terminator plus weird fairy stuff, sent to take Changelings back to the Gentry. They can also grant Changelings Tokens good for one reprieve in exchange for selling out their fellows. Finally, Freeholds are more directly relevant, with a ritual called a Bulwark that forces incoming Huntsmen to follow Approaches in order to chase down Changelings, limiting their methods of attack, but the Bulwark has various requirements that the Freehold has to meet to keep it up.</li> <li>Hunter 2E is also on the way, and it looks like they're restructuring how Endowments work, but again, my laptop is being really bitchy, so I can't actually pull up the preview.</li> <li>Finally, Geist 2E is on the way. There's been very little information yet, as it's still in ultra-early stages. They said something about changing how Sin-Eater Manifestations work, and since ghost rules have changed, I think there's going to be some re-jiggering related to with them ghosts. Also, Geister are now specifically a subset of Rank-3 ghosts, which mostly arise from a ghost drinking from one of the rivers in the Underworld, although it can arise from other causes (once they mentioned that the first person buried in a cemetary arises as its Geistlt guardian).</li> </ul><br /> There's probably a lot more stuff, but I can only write so much in a day, I would recommend that you guy and buy the books and read them. Or borrow from a friend, I guess. But come on, get these guys some money, there's some good shit in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:28:25-07:00","id":1117307,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this counts as minor derailing, but I think it's still relevant to the conversation. Does anyone know where I can find anymore information on that crossover chronicle book? I know it's not on the Monday meeting notes (which are admittedly awesome), but I swore that I heard stuff about it at some point.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also ran a crossover chronicle for a brief period of time, so let me offer some advice on that front.<br /> <br /> It's very difficult to mix all the themes together at one time, so my plan was to explore the themes of the three main splats at various points in the chronicle (I only allowed mages, werewolves, and vampires because I knew those rules better).<br /> <br /> Also, try and sit down with the players when they make a character. That's just a general rule of thumb because that's a good way to find out what the player might want in the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:34:05-07:00","id":1117310,"title":"","content":"There's some information about it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:35:52-07:00","id":1117316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1117294#post1117294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also removed Unihar due to the numerous unfortunate implications, and now the term &quot;Ghost Wolf&quot; refers to Tribeless Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Wolves were always Tribeless werewolves; &quot;unihar&quot; means &quot;Ghost Child.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:43:29-07:00","id":1117327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1116656-compatibility?p=1117316#post1117316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves were always Tribeless werewolves; &quot;unihar&quot; means &quot;Ghost Child.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>: the First Tongue for Ghost Wolf is <i>Thihirtha Numea.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"